  "caption": "Quinn's first netball game: catch, stop, pivot, repeat. Then Quinn landed on someone else's foot and the ankle did a little roll.\n\nBecause you can't run with the ball, netball is full of sudden stops, one-foot landings and pivots. Ankles and knees take much of that load.\n\nWhat often helps: a 15-minute neuromuscular warm-up before play, soft landings with the knee tracking over the toes, single-leg balance work, and strong hamstrings and glutes. Practise sharp changes of direction at training before game day, and fully rehab every sprain.\n\nIf a knee swells, gives way or can't take weight, or an ankle keeps rolling, get it checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
